Patch summary:
Keep the VBR storage VBV fullness from going below zero in the H.264 encoder's
rate control. C2SoftAvcEnc runs libavc in IVE_RC_STORAGE mode. Its buffer,
sized from the level's CPB, gains 4 Mbit per frame (the 240 Mbit/s peak rate
at the nominal 60 fps) and loses each frame's bits.
The fullness had no lower bound, so frames that stayed larger than the inflow
left a growing debt. Full-motion video in a 3456x2160 `ika app` window, with
the QP capped at 18, produced such frames continuously. After 25-35 s the
fullness passed INT32_MIN and the integer-overflow sanitizer aborted
media.swcodec in irc_update_vbr_vbv.

A storage-model decoder stalls on a frame that is larger than its buffer and
resumes with the buffer empty, so the fullness now stops at zero. This also
ends the long stretch at maximum QP that repaying the debt caused once motion
stopped. Streams whose frames fit the buffer are unchanged. The SVC encoder
shares this file.

diff --git a/encoder/irc_vbr_storage_vbv.c b/encoder/irc_vbr_storage_vbv.c
index aaf0d6e..7ea35a5 100644
--- a/encoder/irc_vbr_storage_vbv.c
+++ b/encoder/irc_vbr_storage_vbv.c
@@ -145,7 +145,22 @@ void irc_update_vbr_vbv(vbr_storage_vbv_t *ps_vbr_storage_vbv,
                         ps_vbr_storage_vbv->i4_max_buf_size;
     }
 
-    ps_vbr_storage_vbv->i4_cur_buf_size -= i4_total_bits_decoded;
+    /*
+     * Ika: a VBR storage decoder stalls on a frame larger than its buffer and
+     * resumes empty, so the fullness bottoms out at zero. Letting it go
+     * negative accumulated a debt that kept growing while frames stayed above
+     * the peak inflow (for example a QP ceiling on large full-motion frames),
+     * pinned the QP at its maximum until it was repaid, and finally overflowed
+     * WORD32.
+     */
+    if(i4_total_bits_decoded > ps_vbr_storage_vbv->i4_cur_buf_size)
+    {
+        ps_vbr_storage_vbv->i4_cur_buf_size = 0;
+    }
+    else
+    {
+        ps_vbr_storage_vbv->i4_cur_buf_size -= i4_total_bits_decoded;
+    }
 
     /* Update the error bits state */
     irc_update_error_bits(ps_vbr_storage_vbv->ps_error_bits);
